% ============================================================================
% insulin-glucagon-trigger.query — worked recall queries against
% insulin-glucagon-trigger.adj (adj-facts-stdlib, BIOLOGY).
% ============================================================================
% Three queries: forward recall with citation for each hormone, and a
% backward recall (bind a level, find which hormone responds to it).
%
% EACH ROW ANSWERS WITH ITS OWN SENTENCE (RS-5e, #14986), the locator and
% trust inherited from the table envelope. Until that conversion the envelope
% was the insulin sentence and the glucagon one rode as a `cites`, so a
% glucagon recall was warranted primarily by a sentence about insulin.
%
% The page spells the hormone "glucagons" inside the shipped span; it ships
% verbatim, because citing a sentence the page does not contain is the defect
% that conversion exists to remove.
% ============================================================================

import "insulin-glucagon-trigger.adj"

% Forward: what glucose level triggers insulin release?
? secretion_trigger(insulin, $Level)

% Forward: what glucose level triggers glucagon release?
? secretion_trigger(glucagon, $Level2)

% Backward: which hormone responds to LOW blood glucose?
? secretion_trigger($Hormone, low)
